				104,
				20
			],
			"Message": "feat(Build): Integrate Rhai scripting for profiles and document Wind distribution\n\nThis commit introduces a flexible, script-driven build system using the Rhai language to manage complex build profiles and bundling strategies, while formally documenting the architectural fix for Wind service distribution within the Sky webview.\n\n**Build System Enhancements:**\n\n- Added the `rhai` crate to the root `Cargo.toml`, enabling embedded scripting capabilities for the `Maintain` build tool.\n- Introduced `.vscode/land-config.json` and a suite of Rhai scripts (`.vscode/scripts/profiles/` and `.vscode/scripts/bundler/`) to define distinct build environments (e.g., `oxc-bundle`, `swc-bundle`, `production`, `release`).\n- Updated `Maintain/Debug.sh`, `Maintain/Release.sh`, and added `Maintain/Debug/Wind.sh` to utilize new environment variables (`Level`, `Wind`), providing finer control over build verbosity and specific service inclusion.\n- Added `run_rhai_tests.sh` to validate the syntax and integrity of the new build configuration scripts.\n- Updated `turbo.json` to include `Level` in the pipeline hashing, ensuring build cache invalidation when log levels change.\n\n**Package Management:**\n\n- Added new NPM scripts in `package.json` (e.g., `build:oxc`, `build:swc`, `prepare:bundler`) to execute the `Maintain` binary with specific Rhai profiles.\n- Updated development dependencies (`@playform/build`, `turbo`, `@biomejs/biome`) to their latest versions.\n\n**Architecture & Documentation:**\n\n- Added `Documentation/Architecture/integration/wind-distribution-fix.md`, a comprehensive guide detailing how the `Wind` Effect-TS layer is bundled and resolved as a static dependency in the `Sky` webview. This addresses Vite module resolution issues and the `Static/Wind/` pathing strategy.\n- Updated the `Element` submodule to `fecb6e8d`, which includes the implementation of the Wind distribution fixes and necessary naming refactors to align with the new build tooling.\n\nThis update unifies the build process across the monorepo, allowing for rapid iteration between different bundlers (OXC vs. SWC) and ensures the `Wind` service layer is correctly distributed to the UI.",
			"SHA": "232ce793ad08dca616ee344e0b35143f97524615"
		}
	],
